SUMMARY:Live Jazz: Steve LaSpina Quintet
DESCRIPTION:Celebrated bassist and composer Steve LaSpina has been a vital force on the New York and international jazz scene for more than four decades. A longtime collaborator with icons including Stan Getz\, Benny Carter\, Phil Woods\, Joe Williams\, Clark Terry\, Chet Baker\, Randy Brecker\, Pat Martino\, and Jim Hall\, LaSpina has appeared on more than 275 recordings as both leader and sideman. His recordings as a bandleader and decades of international touring reflect a playing style defined by deep swing\, lyricism\, and musical integrity. For this performance\, LaSpina leads a quartet featuring Dr. Bill Bares\, Jacob Rodriguez\, Tim Fischer\, and Alan Hall\, bringing together seasoned voices for an evening rooted in tradition\, interplay\, and spontaneous exploration. \n$10 at the door (all ticket proceeds are 100% passed to the band\, backed by a living wage guarantee from Hotel Eve) \n*Reserve a table in advance\, or join us impromptu the night of the show. Reservations/advance tickets are recommended for preferred seating\, but not required. Tickets are available at the door on a first-come\, first-served basis.  Event Details and Tickets \nHotel Eve is your locally rooted\, speakeasy jazz club & cocktail bar\, hidden in the heart of Downtown Asheville. Mysteriously not a hotel…check in for spirits\, souls and jazz! We’re tucked away\, on purpose. You’ll find us behind the gate nestled between Virtue Boutique and Dane Wells Gallery at 56 N Lexington Avenue in downtown Asheville. Step through\, take a left into the courtyard\, check in for Spirits\, Souls & Jazz. We’ll be waiting on the other side. hotelevejazz.com \n 
URL:https://livemusicasheville.com/calendar/live-jazz-steve-laspina-quartet/
LOCATION:Hotel Eve Jazz\, 56 N Lexington Avenue\, Asheville\, NC\, 28801\, United States
CATEGORIES:Asheville Area,Live Music
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://livemusicasheville.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/666498073_122126585151134797_5088025641814210026_n-e1776091665350.jpg
